# gen_read_keyed.py: the independent reading landed as a tool, with its exit paths proven
# CM204-Low-2: the exercised leg's independent reading rested on a scratch file, so the evidence was not
# reproducible from the committed record. Same class as the earlier row about a check living outside the tree.
# The parser here is NOT the checker's code and NOT gen_fcov's, deliberately: an independent reading of the same
# report is the whole point, and a second copy of the checker's parser would prove nothing.
# The self-test fabricates a report and three result files, so agreement, a count mismatch and a key absent from
# the report are each OBSERVED rather than reasoned about. Synthetic for the same reason as the identity tool's:
# a test pinned to a real run's counts would fail whenever the stimulus changes.
== 1. --self-test ==
   command: python3 dv/auto_dv/tools/gen_read_keyed.py --self-test
   SELF-TEST ok  the parser reads three bins including a Bins-titled table ({'gen_x_cg.cp_a.hit_a': 7, 'gen_x_cg.cp_a.hit_b': 0, 'gen_x_cg.cp_b.only': 3})
   SELF-TEST ok  agreeing gives rc 0 (want 0)
   SELF-TEST ok  a count mismatch gives rc 1 (want 1)
   SELF-TEST ok  a key absent from the report gives rc 1 (want 1)
   SELF-TEST ok  a run with no derived report gives rc 1 (want 1)
   SELF-TEST: PASS
   rc=0 (want 0)

== 2. the exit paths, each captured DIRECTLY and never through a pipe ==
   no argument                     rc=2 (want 2)
   unknown argument                rc=2 (want 2)
   --self-test with another arg    rc=2 (want 2)
   a directory with no result.yaml rc=2 (want 2)

== 3. against the real nine runs of the exercising run, which is what CM204-Low-2 is about ==
   command: gen_read_keyed.py <the nine isolated run dirs>
     declared 7 | my reading agrees on 7, differs on 0, absent from my reading 0
     declared 10 | my reading agrees on 10, differs on 0, absent from my reading 0
     declared 10 | my reading agrees on 10, differs on 0, absent from my reading 0
     declared 7 | my reading agrees on 7, differs on 0, absent from my reading 0
     declared 10 | my reading agrees on 10, differs on 0, absent from my reading 0
     declared 11 | my reading agrees on 11, differs on 0, absent from my reading 0
     declared 9 | my reading agrees on 9, differs on 0, absent from my reading 0
     declared 8 | my reading agrees on 8, differs on 0, absent from my reading 0
     declared 6 | my reading agrees on 6, differs on 0, absent from my reading 0
   every declared bin agrees with this file's own reading of the report
   rc=0 (want 0)
